@ cases.more-steps-resume-the-body
llvm.unimplemented = "generate: the LLVM backend does not write a `handle` with an arm that keeps its continuation yet"
description = "info.more(m) goes back into the stopped body; what it showed before stopping stays shown once"
source = ```nib
fn count(n: i64): i64 ! {div, overflow} {
  var i := 0
  while i < n { i := i + 1 }
  i
}
let d := handle {
  perform budget(40, () => {
    show(&0)
    count(100)
  })
} with {
  exceeded(info), k => info.more(40)
}
show(&d)
```
stdout = ```
0
100
```

